Your task is to integrate a secure **decentralized authority hierarchy, user authorization system, role-based access control, and metadata-only organizational history** into the existing application.

## 1. CORE ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLE

LANShare remains a **decentralized peer-to-peer LAN application**.

There must be NO permanent central server.

Every PC can continue to communicate directly with another PC.

The architecture must be divided into three logical planes:

### A. CONTENT PLANE

Actual communication and file transfer remain direct peer-to-peer.

Example:

User A
|
| actual message/file
▼
User B

Actual files MUST NOT be replicated to Admin or Supervisor PCs.

Actual chat bodies MUST NOT be replicated to Admin or Supervisor PCs.

Actual photos, videos, audio, documents, attachments, and other media MUST NOT be copied into administrative history.

### B. METADATA / ACTIVITY PLANE

Only encrypted metadata describing communication and transfers may be replicated across authorized/trusted peers.

Example:

Rahul → Priya
PDF
ProjectPlan.pdf
Project Planning
15-09-2026 14:35
Completed

This means the system records that something was shared.

It does NOT replicate the actual content.

### C. AUTHORIZATION PLANE

Implement:

ADMIN
↓
SUPERVISORS
↓
USERS

Authorization must be cryptographically verifiable and must NOT depend only on UI visibility or a role string stored in a local database.

