# 2. ROLES

Implement these roles:

## ADMIN

Exactly ONE permanent organization Admin.

Admin can:

* Create Supervisors
* Remove Supervisors
* Suspend Supervisors
* Revoke Supervisors
* Approve users
* Reject users
* Suspend users
* Revoke users
* Manage trusted devices
* Manage security policies
* Manage authority configuration
* View organization-wide metadata history
* View security events
* View audit logs
* Configure Supervisor permissions
* Manage recovery/failover
* Manage organization authority state

There must never be two permanent ADMIN identities simultaneously.

## SUPERVISOR

Multiple Supervisors are allowed.

Supervisor capabilities must be permission-based.

Potential permissions:

* USER_VIEW
* USER_APPROVE
* USER_REJECT
* USER_SUSPEND
* USER_REVOKE
* DEVICE_VIEW
* DEVICE_APPROVE
* DEVICE_SUSPEND
* DEVICE_REVOKE
* HISTORY_METADATA_VIEW
* AUDIT_VIEW
* SECURITY_EVENT_VIEW

A Supervisor MUST NOT automatically have Admin privileges.

Supervisor MUST NOT be able to:

* Create another permanent Admin
* Remove the permanent Admin
* Change root trust policy
* Change cryptographic root authority
* Arbitrarily modify authority hierarchy
* Grant themselves Admin privileges

unless an explicitly defined failover/acting-admin mechanism permits it.

## USER

Normal organizational user.

User can:

* Send messages
* Receive messages
* Send files
* Receive files
* View their own communication history
* View their own file-transfer history
* Manage permitted personal settings
* View their own account/device status

A USER must NOT be able to view another user's history.

