# 11. CRYPTOGRAPHIC AUTHORIZATION

Authority operations must be signed.

Examples:

ADMIN creates Supervisor
ADMIN approves User
SUPERVISOR approves User
ADMIN revokes Device
ADMIN changes Supervisor permissions

These should produce signed authorization events.

Peers must be able to independently verify:

* Who issued the event
* Whether they had authority
* Whether the signature is valid
* Whether the event is current
* Whether it has already been processed
* Whether it has been revoked
* Whether the authority epoch is valid

