# 18. ENCRYPTED METADATA REPLICATION

Metadata replication must be decentralized.

There is no permanent central database server.

Trusted peers can exchange encrypted metadata events.

Example:

Admin PC
↕
Supervisor PC
↕
Supervisor PC
↕
Trusted peers

Only authorized/trusted peers should receive applicable metadata.

Metadata must be:

* encrypted in transit
* encrypted at rest
* integrity protected
* authenticated
* tamper evident
* replay protected

Possession of the metadata database alone must NOT automatically grant authorization to decrypt or view protected metadata.

Use established cryptographic primitives and libraries.

Do NOT create custom encryption algorithms.

